  { number := 80, text := "" },
  { number := 81, text := "### 3.1 beastdb" },
  { number := 82, text := "" },
  { number := 83, text := "The durable ordered store specified by this document. The name is the lowercase form defined in Clause 1.3." },
  { number := 84, text := "" },
  { number := 85, text := "### 3.2 libbeastdb" },
  { number := 86, text := "" },
  { number := 87, text := "The freestanding product library for beastdb. It is the prefix lib plus the lowercase product name. It is the library that high assurance persistent storage targets (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 88, text := "" },
  { number := 89, text := "### 3.3 Systems Lean" },
  { number := 90, text := "" },
  { number := 91, text := "The language specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md): Lean 4 with linear and affine ownership and Quantitative Type Theory multiplicities 0, 1, and omega." },
  { number := 92, text := "" },
  { number := 93, text := "### 3.4 Slake" },
  { number := 94, text := "" },
  { number := 95, text := "The compiler specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md): the compiler written in Systems Lean that emits freestanding products." },
  { number := 96, text := "" },
  { number := 97, text := "### 3.5 Freestanding product library" },
  { number := 98, text := "" },
  { number := 99, text := "A library binary or C source emitted by Slake that contains no managed Lean runtime and performs no garbage collection, matching the freestanding product wire in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md)." },
  { number := 100, text := "" },
  { number := 101, text := "### 3.6 Proven ACID" },
  { number := 102, text := "" },
  { number := 103, text := "Atomicity, consistency, isolation, and durability as machine checked properties of the store, not as marketing language. This document requires those properties of a conforming implementation. This document is not those proofs, and it does not claim the proofs exist yet." },
  { number := 104, text := "" },
  { number := 105, text := "### 3.7 Trie that does not use locks" },
  { number := 106, text := "" },
  { number := 107, text := "A trie in which progress of a reader or writer does not depend on another thread being scheduled to release a mutual exclusion lock on that trie. This document requires a conforming implementation to use tries that do not use locks. It does not claim such tries are implemented." },
  { number := 108, text := "" },
  { number := 109, text := "### 3.8 SWMR" },
  { number := 110, text := "" },
  { number := 111, text := "Single writer, multiple reader. One writer at a time, with concurrent readers. This is the required default concurrency for a conforming implementation." },
  { number := 112, text := "" },
  { number := 113, text := "### 3.9 Fencing by generation" },
  { number := 114, text := "" },
  { number := 115, text := "A discipline in which structural operations (rebalance, relocate, map growth, and similar) carry a generation so that a reader cannot observe torn structure from a prior generation as if it were current." },
  { number := 116, text := "" },
  { number := 117, text := "### 3.10 Schema" },
  { number := 118, text := "" },
  { number := 119, text := "A declared structure for keys, values, and related types stored by beastdb. Schema is mandatory (Clause 4.4). This document defines two modes: predefined and inferred." },
  { number := 120, text := "" },
  { number := 121, text := "### 3.11 Predefined schema" },
  { number := 122, text := "" },
  { number := 123, text := "A schema declared before data that uses it is written." },
  { number := 124, text := "" },
  { number := 125, text := "### 3.12 Inferred schema" },
  { number := 126, text := "" },
  { number := 127, text := "A schema derived from stored data and then declared so later access and migration can be proved against it. Inferred is a mode of mandatory schema, not a license to remain without a schema." },
  { number := 128, text := "" },
  { number := 129, text := "### 3.13 fargo" },
  { number := 130, text := "" },
  { number := 131, text := "The Surmount interoperability layer to be specified in a later numbered specification. fargo has no assigned specification number. That specification has not been published and this document does not assign it a shipped version. Compatibility with other stores and language ecosystems SHALL go through fargo (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 132, text := "" },
  { number := 133, text := "### 3.14 LanguageID" },
  { number := 134, text := "" },
  { number := 135, text := "A dense identifier for a language in the store. It is not a Unicode code point used as the primary key." },
  { number := 136, text := "" },
  { number := 137, text := "### 3.15 WordID" },
  { number := 138, text := "" },
  { number := 139, text := "A dense identifier for a word in the store. It is not a Unicode code point used as the primary key." },
  { number := 140, text := "" },
  { number := 141, text := "### 3.16 Rosetta" },
  { number := 142, text := "" },
  { number := 143, text := "A mapping between LanguageID and WordID values across languages, persisted so the Smart Symbolic Supercompiler specified in `0004_SSSSS.md` can use dense symbols." },
  { number := 144, text := "" },
  { number := 145, text := "### 3.17 Requirement keywords" },
  { number := 146, text := "" },
  { number := 147, text := "The key words MUST, MUST NOT, REQUIRED, SHALL, SHALL NOT, SHOULD, SHOULD NOT, RECOMMENDED, MAY, and OPTIONAL in this document are to be interpreted as described in RFC 2119." },
  { number := 148, text := "" },
  { number := 149, text := "### 3.18 Slake that fully typechecks" },
  { number := 150, text := "" },
  { number := 151, text := "A bootstrapped Slake compiler that typechecks the Systems Lean and Slake sources it is bootstrapped from, including theorems, as defined in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 3.10. A named subset of modules is not enough. Emitting freestanding C without that typecheck is not enough." },
  { number := 152, text := "" },
  { number := 153, text := "### 3.19 CompCert verified compilation" },
  { number := 154, text := "" },
  { number := 155, text := "Compilation of the freestanding C emit by CompCert (`ccomp`) such that the generated assembly is the CompCert verified compilation of that C, as defined in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 3.9." },
  { number := 156, text := "" },
  { number := 157, text := "### 3.20 Traditional foreign function interface" },
  { number := 158, text := "" },
  { number := 159, text := "A language native binding layer that calls into libbeastdb (or a shim) through the host platform calling convention as the primary interoperability path. This document forbids that path as the interoperability path (Clause 4.5). fargo is the interoperability path." },
  { number := 160, text := "" },
  { number := 161, text := "## 4. Core requirements" },
  { number := 162, text := "" },
  { number := 163, text := "### 4.1 Language, bootstrap, freestanding library, and name" },
  { number := 164, text := "" },
  { number := 165, text := "1. The core of beastdb MUST be implemented in Systems Lean as specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md)." },
  { number := 166, text := "2. That core MUST be able to target the freestanding Slake path in that specification." },
  { number := 167, text := "3. libbeastdb MUST be a freestanding product library: it MUST contain no managed Lean runtime and MUST NOT perform garbage collection." },
  { number := 168, text := "4. The product name and library name MUST follow Clause 1.3." },
  { number := 169, text := "5. CompCert verified compilation (Clause 3.19) is a REQUIRED core validation step for the freestanding C emit of that core, as required by [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 4.2 item 6. Naming a residual MUST NOT substitute for this step. This document does not claim CompCert is pinned under this specifications repository's `ref/`." },
  { number := 170, text := "6. Bootstrapping a Slake compiler that fully typechecks (Clause 3.18) is a REQUIRED core validation step, as required by [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 4.2 item 7. A conforming build MUST use a Slake that typechecks the Systems Lean and Slake sources it is bootstrapped from, including theorems. A named subset of modules is not enough. Naming a residual MUST NOT substitute for this step. A claim that the freestanding product hosts itself from generated C is a distinct claim and does not satisfy this step by itself." },
  { number := 171, text := "" },
  { number := 172, text := "### 4.2 Proven ACID, tries that do not use locks, concurrency, and fencing by generation" },
  { number := 173, text := "" },
  { number := 174, text := "1. A conforming implementation MUST provide proven ACID transactions (Clause 3.6). This is a requirement. This document does not claim those proofs have been written." },
  { number := 175, text := "2. The durable map MUST be a trie that does not use locks (Clause 3.7). This is a requirement. This document does not claim such a trie is implemented." },
  { number := 176, text := "3. The required default concurrency MUST be SWMR (Clause 3.8)." },
  { number := 177, text := "4. A conforming implementation MAY provide more than one writer, each operating only on disjoint leaves of the trie. That capability is optional. It is not required for conformance. When it is absent, SWMR remains required. When it is present, writers MUST NOT share a leaf." },
  { number := 178, text := "5. Structural operations MUST be fenced by generation (Clause 3.9). This is a requirement. This document does not claim fencing by generation is implemented." },
  { number := 179, text := "" },
  { number := 180, text := "### 4.3 Memory mapping, SIMD, zerocopy, and dense identifiers" },
  { number := 181, text := "" },
  { number := 182, text := "1. A conforming implementation MUST use memory mapping (mmap) for the durable image." },
  { number := 183, text := "2. A conforming implementation MUST use single instruction, multiple data (SIMD) facilities for scans and bulk operations where those facilities improve those operations. The instruction set family is defined by the implementation." },
  { number := 184, text := "3. A conforming implementation MUST offer zerocopy views of mapped data for reads. A bounce buffer MUST NOT be required for a read that can be served by a mapped view." },
  { number := 185, text := "4. A conforming implementation MUST persist dense LanguageID and WordID values (Clauses 3.14 and 3.15)." },
  { number := 186, text := "5. A Rosetta mapping (Clause 3.16) for the Smart Symbolic Supercompiler specified in `0004_SSSSS.md` MUST be representable in the store." },
  { number := 187, text := "6. Items 1 through 5 are requirements. This document does not claim mmap, SIMD, zerocopy, LanguageID, WordID, or Rosetta are implemented." },
  { number := 188, text := "" },
  { number := 189, text := "### 4.4 Mandatory schema" },
  { number := 190, text := "" },
  { number := 191, text := "1. Schema is mandatory. A conforming implementation MUST NOT offer a product mode that stores application data without a schema." },
  { number := 192, text := "2. A conforming implementation MUST support both predefined schema (Clause 3.11) and inferred schema (Clause 3.12)." },
  { number := 193, text := "3. Inferred schema MUST become a declared schema. Inference MUST NOT leave data permanently without a schema." },
  { number := 194, text := "4. Every migration MUST be proven. A migration that cannot be proved MUST NOT be applied." },
  { number := 195, text := "5. Items 1 through 4 are requirements. This document does not claim schema proofs exist yet." },
  { number := 196, text := "" },
  { number := 197, text := "### 4.5 Access patterns and interoperability" },
  { number := 198, text := "" },
  { number := 199, text := "1. A conforming implementation MUST provide access by ordered keys and values." },
  { number := 200, text := "2. A conforming implementation MUST provide time series access." },
  { number := 201, text := "3. A conforming implementation MUST provide vector access." },
  { number := 202, text := "4. Compatibility with SQLite, RocksDB, and other stores named as prior art in Clause 2.3, and compatibility with other language ecosystems, SHALL be expressed through fargo (Clause 3.13; unpublished; no assigned specification number)." },
  { number := 203, text := "5. A conforming implementation MUST NOT use a traditional foreign function interface (Clause 3.20) as the interoperability path. There is no traditional foreign function binding layer in this design. Interoperability goes through fargo." },
  { number := 204, text := "6. Exact layout of time series points and vectors is defined by the implementation provided items 1 through 3 hold." },
  { number := 205, text := "7. Items 1 through 5 are requirements. This document does not claim access by ordered keys and values, time series access, vector access, or fargo shims are implemented. fargo itself has no numbered specification file in this repository." },
  { number := 206, text := "" },
  { number := 207, text := "### 4.6 Stack role" },
  { number := 208, text := "" },
  { number := 209, text := "1. beastdb is the REQUIRED durable store for the Smart Symbolic Supercompiler specified in `0004_SSSSS.md`." },
  { number := 210, text := "2. All high assurance persistent storage that claims conformance to this stack role MUST target libbeastdb." },
  { number := 211, text := "3. Systems Lean remains the REQUIRED implementation language for the core of beastdb, as stated in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 4.4." },
  { number := 212, text := "" },
  { number := 213, text := "### 4.7 Store that is local first; network features out of scope" },
  { number := 214, text := "" },
  { number := 215, text := "1. beastdb is a store that is local first: a conforming implementation MUST operate as a local durable store without requiring a network peer." },
  { number := 216, text := "2. Network peering is out of scope for this specification." },
  { number := 217, text := "3. Replication is out of scope for this specification." },
  { number := 218, text := "4. High availability as a distributed property is out of scope for this specification." },
  { number := 219, text := "5. Distribution of the store across machines is out of scope for this specification." },
  { number := 220, text := "6. Those network topics belong to the Carbonado Network Protocol. That protocol has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Discussion has mentioned 0006 as a possible later number. This document does not assign 0006. This document MUST NOT be read as specifying peering, replication, high availability, or distribution." },
  { number := 221, text := "" },
  { number := 222, text := "## 5. Conformance" },
  { number := 223, text := "" },
  { number := 224, text := "A beastdb implementation or libbeastdb product conforms to this specification if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 225, text := "" },
  { number := 226, text := "1. It uses the lowercase product name beastdb and the library name libbeastdb (Clause 1.3). The core is implemented in Systems Lean, targets the freestanding Slake path, and libbeastdb is a freestanding product library (Clause 4.1 items 1 through 4)." },
  { number := 227, text := "2. CompCert verified compilation of the freestanding C emit has been performed (Clause 4.1 item 5). A bootstrapped Slake compiler fully typechecks the Systems Lean and Slake sources it is bootstrapped from (Clause 4.1 item 6). A named subset of modules is not enough. Naming a residual MUST NOT substitute for either step." },
  { number := 228, text := "3. It provides proven ACID transactions, tries that do not use locks, SWMR, and structural operations fenced by generation (Clause 4.2 items 1, 2, 3, and 5). More than one writer on disjoint leaves MAY be present (Clause 4.2 item 4) and is not required." },
  { number := 229, text := "4. It uses mmap, SIMD as required, and zerocopy reads, and it persists LanguageID, WordID, and a representable Rosetta mapping (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 230, text := "5. Schema is mandatory, both predefined and inferred modes are supported, inferred schema becomes declared, and every migration is proven (Clause 4.4)." },
  { number := 231, text := "6. It provides access by ordered keys and values, time series access, and vector access; interoperability goes through fargo and not through a traditional foreign function interface; and high assurance persistent storage that claims this stack role targets libbeastdb (Clauses 4.5 and 4.6)." },
  { number := 232, text := "" },
  { number := 233, text := "Optional access by more than one writer on disjoint leaves (Clause 4.2 item 4) is not required for conformance." },
  { number := 234, text := "" },
  { number := 235, text := "Network peering, replication, high availability, and distribution (Clause 4.7) are out of scope. An implementation that offers those features may still conform to this specification only for the local store. Those features are not conformance items here and MUST NOT be claimed as this specification." },
  { number := 236, text := "" },
  { number := 237, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming implementation. Meeting these items is a claim about a product, not about this markdown file." },
  { number := 238, text := "" },
  { number := 239, text := "## 6. Residual" },
  { number := 240, text := "" },
  { number := 241, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. It does not add product behavior beyond Clauses 4 and 5. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, an unpinned prior art name, an unimplemented requirement, or an out of scope network feature named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. The repository root `RESIDUAL.md` restates residual for the numbered specification program; this clause is the residual record for this specification." },
  { number := 242, text := "" },
  { number := 243, text := "### 6.1 Related specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 244, text := "" },
  { number := 245, text := "1. The Smart Symbolic Supercompiler is specified in `0004_SSSSS.md`. That specification does not claim a conforming SSSSS implementation exists." },
  { number := 246, text := "2. fargo has no assigned specification number. A previous plan that assigned number 0005 to fargo is withdrawn. Number 0005 is Concise American Technical English (`0005_CATE.md`). Number 0006 is Recursive Self Improvement (`0006_RSI.md`). This document does not invent a new number for fargo. Clause 4.5 names fargo as the interoperability path; that is a requirement on a future product, not a claim that fargo is specified or implemented." },
  { number := 247, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol is deferred. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Discussion has mentioned 0006 as a possible later number. That mention is not an assignment. This document does not create a file for it." },
